+  PASS  S1f player final kill on Bajora still unlocks feat and >= +15 Cardassian
+  PASS  S2a hunter keeps pursuing beyond weapon range
+  PASS  S2b hunter beyond weapon range never fires (weapon ready, >2 cooldowns)
+  PASS  S2c hunter inside weapon range fires and lands (beam)
+  PASS  S3a Breen and Dominion have no declared relationship either way
+  PASS  S3a five formerly missing keys are present in the table as empty lists
+  PASS  S3a unknown relation key warns exactly once
+  PASS  S3b foreign-owned and private stations in the player system keep their owners
+  PASS  S3b independent escort and owned station both fire on a raider (ticks)
+  PASS  S3b hostile independent ship is a target and attacker; independence is no immunity
+  PASS  S3c neutral trader never defends
+  PASS  S3c same-flag foreign patrol may assist a raid defense while staying foreign
+  PASS  S3c a hostile station flying the player flag is an escort target; a calm one is not
+  PASS  S3c same-flag foreign vessel that fires on the player station is an attacker and target
+  PASS  S3d raising a flag re-flags owned installations only; owners unchanged
+  PASS  S3d same-flag raid: player escorts wearing the raider flag still count and engage
+  PASS  S3e peaceful foreign patrol is not a defender against a fleet it has no quarrel with
+  PASS  S3e a foreign concession at war with the raiders counts as a defender until reduced
+  PASS  S3e real raid capture transfers control and player installations, not the foreign station
+  PASS  S3e a surviving occupation fleet blocks reclamation; clearing it allows the claim
+  PASS  S3e the real Claim button reclaims control and installations without re-flagging the foreign station (runtime and cache)
+  PASS  S3f unknown origin stays unknown (no controller, no polity)
+  PASS  S3f custom polity ID is preserved exactly (case included)
+  PASS  S3f custom polity ships and station share one side; an unrelated independent does not
+  PASS  S3f explicit independence is distinct per world and never the origin empire
+  PASS  S3g arrival protection is personal (fleet, orders, factions, control, stations untouched)
+  PASS  S3h control for every planet is identical across save/reload
+  PASS  S3h expected holders after reload (player, independent Earth, Cardassian Bajora, untouched origins)
+  PASS  S3h station owners and flags survive reload and re-entry
+  PASS  S3h legacy save without ownership records migrates to the expected owners
+  PASS  S3k cached re-entry keeps existing ship id, hull, faction and side across return and change of holder
+  PASS  S3k a constructed custom-polity ship in the snapshot is not re-fitted on restoration
+  PASS  S3l flying the holder flag is not control, but grants faction access
